A||||42||Cliff Pennock||Where are all the Fieros?
Z||000000||Cliff Pennock||08-06-99||06:37 AM||||Hey everyone!<p>It's my last day in the States today and I finally got my hands on a computer so I can post a message again. Anyway, After three weeks of Pennsylvania (and one day Canada) I have only seen 5 Fieros - four 84 models and one 85 model. I was expecting to see a lot more than that... So where are all the Fieros? Is it really such a rare car here?
Z||000001||DJRice||08-06-99||06:52 AM||||Cliff, <p>I cant speak for everybody, but I think maybe it is.  I just moved to Titusville, FL about 3 months ago.  "Space Coast Fieros" is around here somewhere, a relativley large club, or so I thought, and I have only seen 3 different Fieros since Ive been here.
Z||000002||87GT||08-06-99||07:03 AM||||Cliff, I live in the Tampa Bay area.  The last few days, I have driven to Tampa, and Lakeland and have not seen ANY fieros.  I was the only one around.  Whenever I do see a fiero, its usually the notchback 84-87 models.  They are usually in bad shape.  The last time I saw a GT was about 3 weeks ago in Mulberry.  I think they are beginning to get fairly rare.
Z||000003||ChadMan||08-06-99||07:33 AM||||Yeah, I think the fastback GT's are starting to be squirreled away in people's garages.  I see a lot of Fieros around central Ohio, but it seems like most of them are red 84s with bad paint and headlights stuck open.<p>Did see a beautiful 87 blue coupe with aftermarket wheels last night in traffic though.  He waved, I waved back...it's a beautiful thing.
Z||000004||theogre||08-06-99||08:33 AM||||there are a few around here, even a couple for sale. There's a GT over in NJ for sale even.<p>They are starting to get rare....... 
Z||000005||four50four||08-06-99||10:05 AM||||never ever in my whole life have i seen a fiero GT fastback. if i do see a notchback chances are its a red 84. seen 3 different V6's. 
Z||000006||Formula||08-06-99||10:16 AM||||I live in western PA and I see at least one fiero every day (mine)LOL. There is a white 88gt with blue stripes and 17" tri-star wheels on it around here, about 5 red 2m4s, a blue se 4cyl (it has a gt front and se badges(very perty)), I've never seen a black fiero in person. 
Z||000007||Bruce||08-06-99||11:22 AM||||Better for us Fiero owners, as we watch our cars become collector items!
Z||000008||lowCG||08-06-99||12:02 PM||||I see more sitting in yards than on the road,just saw a really nice fastback yesterday in Gig Harbor though,some exhaust work,big wing thing.
Z||000009||Cliff Pennock||08-06-99||12:02 PM||||I also noticed that if I tell people what kind of car I drive, they respond with "a Pontiac <b>what</b>?". :)
Z||000010||DJRice||08-06-99||12:15 PM||||Did you guys ever notice that everybody seems to have a story about a Fiero?  They either had one or knew someone who did.  Everytime I  used to go into my local auto parts store, the same guy at the parts counter would always say "My buddy had one of those SOBs.  He had to start it everyday with starting fluid, it ran fine once you got it running..."<p>In the same store, they hired a new kid at the checkout counter and he asked me "Is it true that you have to pull the engine to change the spark plugs?"<p>My response was "Only if you have the V-6, and you want to change <b>all</b> the spark plugs."<p>
Z||000011||DaRkLoRD||08-06-99||12:34 PM||||There are a few Fieros in my town, a black 86 SE (I was looking at it at the dealership last summer, but it was a bit too expensive for me..), a silver GT (don't know which year), and a red notchback, I'm not sure which model it is. There's also a brown notchback around here somewhere, but I don't see it too often. I've also seen a modified Fiero about an hour and a half away from my town, towards Toronto, that looked like it had 4x4 suspension.. was about 3'-4' off the ground, huge wheels.. someone posted pictures of something similar to this forum.<p>I went to Alberta for a week this summer, and saw only a couple Fieros.. one was a nice looking yellow GT that I saw just going into B.C. I don't even remember what the other one was.. didn't catch my attention..<p>I'd have to agree, Fieros aren't too common anymore. Not in this area at least.
Z||000012||Patrick||08-06-99||01:02 PM||||<br>Well, I guess you guys will have to visit <b>Vancouver BC</b>. Fieros of all types are EVERYWHERE here. I'm not kidding.<p>When I bought mine two years ago, there were four in my neighborhood within a ONE block radius.<p>
Z||000013||Eric||08-06-99||04:47 PM||||It sounds like I will have a one of a kind Fiero when I finish converting my black 88GT into a 3.2.  I'm thinking of putting small stickers behind the front wheels that say 3.2, so everyone who is in the Columbus, Ohio area knows that's my Fiero. <p>There are a few other "rare" type Fieros in the COFE club and I look foward to seeing them at the Nationals here next week.
Z||000014||Cooter||08-06-99||07:55 PM||||I guess that I am lucky here in the south east US because we are eat up with these cars! There are several around on car lots and plenty in back yards with weeds growing up around them. I wish that I had the funds to buy everyone of them and start my own "farm". One day these things will be like owning gold. . .
