Z||000016||Nick||08-06-99||09:20 PM||||Well, here in Michigan, there are buttloads of 'em.  Makes sense since they were built here.  It makes me sick to see all the beat up and neglected Fieros in the Detroit and Flint areas.  I'm over in Grand Rapids, and there are still quite a few over here.  I probably see anywhere from 5 to 10 each day.<p>Every once in a while, I'll see a real nice fastback GT, but none nicer than mine. :-)<p>There are a couple of 88 GT's with T-tops and real low miles for sale over here.  Both red, both pretty pricey, but real nice.  One has like 6000 actual miles! <p>
Z||000017||kel||08-06-99||11:20 PM||||I live in south central Pa.  There are times when weeks can go by without ever seeing another Fiero.  I did happen to see a nice looking red GT today, but that is rare.  Most of the ones I see, are not in very good shape.  Makes me want to take even better care of mine.     
Z||000018||G25C||08-06-99||11:51 PM||||I live in North west Ohio and i havent seen too many myself.  A red one sets in a yard down the road.  A black one sits in town winking permanently.  I saw a black one on a flat bed (looked like a bomb went off in it).  All were notch back.  I havnt seen any fast back GT's lately.  <br>   I know around my town (back when Fieros were being made) a family down the road had 3 new ones.  Then one bad winter day around Christmas, the mom and pop were leaving town and went out of control on the road (weather was horrible that day) and were ran over by a semi truck and killed instantly.<p>  Ever sence then everyone i know in a 50 mile radius calls the Fiero a death trap!  And most folks dont have anything good to say about them. (although they themselves have never owned one).<p>One time a lady told me she loved my car and thought it was cool!  Then she wanted to know what kind of HONDA (!!!??) it was!  After i told her it was a Pontiac Fiero.  She shrieked and said "im not getting near that time bomb!"<p>Hey! Dont Knock it till ya try it!!<p>Am i right folks??
Z||000019||Racer 1||08-07-99||03:03 AM||||Here in Alamogordo,New Mexico theres about 5-10 fiero's driving around mostly notch backs and a black 87 GT sunroof full hop-ups for sale real cheap 2000.00$.Theres one 85 v-6 notch back in town that isnt well main tained and every time I see it I makes me angry at a PERFECT car wasted.Also theres this PUNK kid thats always trying to race me even though I have beat him acouple of times "On a a-ban-done road"A.K.A dragstrip.The people who usually by the fiero's sell them after a few months especialy the nothcback versions.All the GT's still have the original owners from back when I got my BLESSED coupe-de-vill.But my fiero the best looking fiero in town.Thats becuase I have bonded with my fiero thru thick and thin.And sometimes the thins come in one massive wave multi problems all at once.HEHE....I always get complements and looks from other people clueless to what kinda car there looking at.Well thats my storie and sticky to it!PEACE!
Z||000020||87GT||08-07-99||05:28 PM||||It makes me wonder why people call them time bombs.  I have heard that the Fiero had excellent crash test ratings.  I am sure everyone here has heard about the young lady that had her car dragged 4 miles by a freight train and lived to tell the story.  She was driving a FIERO!  I saw a picture of her car, there wasnt much left, but she survived without major injury.  I think that speaks enough for the Fiero.  BTW, I saw a fiero today, it was a white 84 2M4.  First one I have seen in a while.  
Z||000021||Ozzy||08-07-99||11:02 PM||||I'm in the North West and have seen several different Fieros, not to mention the '88 coupe I bought here. Couple of coupes and GT's. Don't know what years...still getting familiar with all the blurb. This web site helps a bunch I might add. Sad to say there have been 2 dead Fiero's on the side of the interstate in the last month. Every one I told about buying a Fiero would remark "oh oh...watch out! It's gonna catch on fire and blow up and crash into shit and a big monster's hand is gonna come out from under the seat while yer drivin' and tear your intestines out and throw 'em out the window!!!" Damn I've heard it all from people who, guess what, HAVE NEVER OWNED ONE!! Anyway, I've surmised that regular attention and maintenance are really important but thats fine by me. I luv driving this car.<p>Ozzy
Z||000022||Dave85||08-08-99||02:26 PM||||I live in northwest Arkansas and there are only a few Fieros in the area. There are a couple for sale dirt cheap and soon they will be mine. The mentality is the same here, people think I'm nuts for having one. There are used car lots every 1/4 mile here and if and when they get one, they dump them CHEAP!!! The funny thing is, one day they're gonna wish they had one.
Z||000023||DaRkLoRD||08-08-99||04:55 PM||||I wish it was like that around here.. A friend of mine used to work at a local GM dealership, and one day he called me and said there was a Fiero for sale there. I went up and had a look, 86 SE. interior wasn't in great condition, seats were ripped, etc. They wanted over $4k for it.. (cdn)<p>If I had that much, I might pay it for a decent GT.. but that car would need a lot of work to make me pay that much for it. This was last year, and last month, the same person told me he saw the Fiero down at the beach.. Whoever bought it had cut the top off and made it a convertible. He said they weren't finished yet, as he could still see the cut marks.. hadn't been finished yet with body filler, painted, etc.
Z||000024||PaUL||08-09-99||02:41 AM||||I live in Hawaii and see at least 1 other fiero on the road everyday. I cant believe you people on the mainland dont see too many. I guess part of the reason why fiero are so cheap are the perceptions people have of this car. Most probably think its a really crappy car and the biggest mistake GM made in the 80s. On the other hand, maybe they are so scarce because some of the perceptions are true. 
Z||000025||Harry||08-09-99||08:21 PM||||Im sorry for some off you,<br>Here in sunny VA Beach and surrounding Hampton roads we have about 70-80 off them running around.<br>Each day I see a different car somewhere.<br>Of course there are the few like us who have "BONDED" then theres the #$%^& cars that give the rest a bad name.<br>Check out our clubs web page to see somne of the nicer ones<br>F.O.C.O.S.E.V.A.
