Z||000027||RossT||08-12-99||12:27 AM||||I see lots of 2m4's around here (Bismarck<br>North Dakota). Only seen one gt in the<br>past 6 months. There are lots of fieros in<br>the junk yards. People around here don't<br>think much of the fiero.  (their loss).<p>Hey overlord, if you get down this way look<br>me up.  It would be nice to talk to another<br>"fieronut" in person.
Z||000028||RFMike||08-14-99||07:59 AM||||There are 5 in my hometown of 10,000.  I work in Minneapolis, and see 4 or 5 each week.   That's not counting the 2 red notchbacks that park in the same lot as I do (not the same lot where I got trashed).  (Eric, do you park by Washington and 1st Ave?  One of them has a U of M sticker).  Haven't parked at the same time as them, so haven't talked.  Passed a black GT that looked to be a twin of mine a couple of weeks ago.  Got the thumbs up for the first time from another Fiero owner.  There are quite a few around here, and the prices are mostly high.  Most of them look to be pretty well maintained, at least on the outside.  <br>I make a site visit to a really small town in western minnesota twice a month for a school we're doing there.  While I was parked, one of the residents drove up and told me his son was really excited about seeing my car.  He had driven a friend's, got hooked, and had just bought the fourth one in this town of 1,000.  They are out there, and those that own em love em.
Z||000029||batboy||08-14-99||09:08 AM||||I've noticed that in the last couple of years most of the nicer Fieros are getting less driving time and more garage time around here in NE Kansas. I still see several one-eyed beat up Fieros. One young lady I talked to in the laundromat the other day that had a 86 Fiero that looked like a demolition derby car. I've seen better looking Fieros in the salvage yards. She admitted that "she was a little hard on her car" so I decided not to ask her out. Heck, she might be a little hard on men too, ya never know. Besides, I saw that crazy "I want to wreck your car too" look in eyes when she scoping out my Batmobile.
