Z||000040||ChadMan||08-26-99||07:57 AM||||A West Virginia couple sends their daughter to Ohio State.  Four years later, they make the drive to Columbus to see her graduate, but get lost on Ohio State's giant campus.  After driving around for almost an hour, they see a professorial-looking fellow walking along and decide to ask him for directions.<p>"'Scuse me, sir," the West Virginian fellow asks, "but can you tell me where the stadium is at?"<p>The professor looks at the West Virginians with disdain.  "My friends, this is the Ohio State University, an internationally-renowned center of higher learning, and we don't end our sentences with prepositions."<p>The West Virginian shrugs and says, "Oh, sorry, sir.  Could you tell me where the stadium is at, asshole?"
